2026-11-12  Jaipaul Cheernam <jaipaul.cheernam@est.tech>

	* m4/groff.m4 (GROFF_G): Apply the "g" command prefix only when
	the troff on PATH runs and reports a non-GNU ".g" value, not
	whenever its output differs from "1".  A troff that is installed
	but fails to run--as the native groff does when cross
	compiling, lacking its device files--is no longer mistaken for
	a groff-incompatible troff.

	[An existing troff program might fail to produce any output if
	it's compiled (a) for a different ABI or (b) with ASAN and
	`ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0` is not in the environment.  Owing
	to its age, GNU troff has lots of memory leaks and cleaning them
	up is a long-term project.  (This is likely true of other troffs
	as well.)

	Fixes <https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?686901.  Problem
	introduced by me in commit 96b8274a90, 14 October, itself a
	follow-up to commit 142b8d93fc, 8 October.  Evidently this stuff
	is harder than it looks.  --GBR]

